reference_solutions.javascript:
function isValid(s) {
  // Push the closer we expect next; every closer must match the top.
  const expect = { '(': ')', '[': ']', '{': '}' };
  const stack = [];
  for (const ch of s) {
    if (ch in expect) stack.push(expect[ch]);
    else if (stack.pop() !== ch) return false;
  }
  return stack.length === 0;
}

editorial_md:
### Intuition
The most recently opened bracket must be the first one closed — last in, first out. That is exactly a stack.

### Algorithm
Scan the string. Push every opening bracket. For a closing bracket, the stack must be non-empty and its top must be the matching opener; pop it. At the end the stack must be empty (nothing left unclosed).

```python
def isValid(s):
    pairs = {')': '(', ']': '[', '}': '{'}
    stack = []
    for ch in s:
        if ch in pairs:
            if not stack or stack[-1] != pairs[ch]:
                return False
            stack.pop()
        else:
            stack.append(ch)
    return not stack
```

### Complexity
O(n) time and O(n) space in the worst case (all openers).

